   "design": "Cancer reports use structured templates that follow the national protocols: the pathologist enters each value once in the protocol fields, and the template writes the matching text, instead of retyping values from the text. The lab system fills patient, specimen, prior report and clinical data into the report. Diagnosis codes are suggested from the conclusion, each with the phrase it rests on, and the pathologist confirms every code. The lab system worklist replaces the spreadsheet of pending reports. Dictation, correcting the text, the conclusion, resident review, authorisation, release and queries stay with the pathologist.",
